# Keep shell hooks on LF line endings on every platform.
#
# Claude Code runs the hooks in .claude/hooks/ with bash. On Windows, git's
# default core.autocrlf=true would check them out with CRLF endings, and bash
# then fails with "$'\r': command not found" - the credentials-commit guard
# silently stops protecting you. Pinning eol=lf prevents that.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same for the git hooks in .githooks/. `pre-commit` has no extension, so the rule
# above would miss it — and a CRLF pre-commit hook fails the same silent way.
.githooks/* text eol=lf
